WEBVTT

00:00.619 --> 00:03.844
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:03.944 --> 00:07.212
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:07.248 --> 00:10.783
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:10.818 --> 00:13.786
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:13.821 --> 00:17.289
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:17.324 --> 00:20.592
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:20.628 --> 00:22.161
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:22.196 --> 00:23.529
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:23.564 --> 00:23.597
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:34.108 --> 00:35.841
Hey, great idea bringing
the couch out here

00:35.876 --> 00:37.576
from your den, Peter.
Yeah, Lois and I

00:37.611 --> 00:39.878
dragged it out here last night
for a little hump sesh,

00:39.913 --> 00:41.480
so I figured I'd let it dry.

00:41.515 --> 00:43.448
"Couch." That's
one of those words

00:43.484 --> 00:46.585
that if you say it over and over
it starts to sound silly.

00:46.620 --> 00:48.920
Joe, you need to take
a class on small talk.

00:48.956 --> 00:51.590
You're not gonna believe
this-- I'm in one.

00:51.625 --> 00:53.825
It sure is cloudy today.

00:53.861 --> 00:56.361
Good. You could have
also responded to Janet,

00:56.397 --> 00:58.397
who said her son died.

00:58.432 --> 01:02.234
I'm sorry your son died
on such a cloudy day.

01:07.274 --> 01:09.207
All right, kids,
here's your bacon.

01:09.243 --> 01:11.610
I call the paper towel!
Aw, damn it!

01:11.645 --> 01:14.646
Ha-ha! You got to move fast
when Meg's at the table, Brian.

01:14.681 --> 01:17.582
All right, well, I get the box
when we have pizza for dinner.

01:17.618 --> 01:19.384
Uh-uh. It
doesn't work that way.

01:19.420 --> 01:21.520
You got to call it
when it's happening.

01:21.555 --> 01:23.155
Good morning, family.
I'll be out front

01:23.190 --> 01:24.823
with the guys
if anybody needs me.

01:24.858 --> 01:26.491
Peter, I thought
we were gonna try

01:26.527 --> 01:28.393
to get the garden going
again today.

01:28.429 --> 01:31.930
I know, sweetie, but then
I realized how stupid that is.

01:31.965 --> 01:34.766
Okay, bye. You guys
are my everything.

01:34.802 --> 01:36.301
Why'd you ever marry him?

01:36.336 --> 01:39.771
Believe it or not, he used to
look like a young Gene Hackman.

01:39.807 --> 01:42.707
That's... that-that's
not even good.

01:42.743 --> 01:43.909
It's gone!

01:43.944 --> 01:45.243
What? What's gone?

01:45.279 --> 01:47.779
Our drinking couch!
Somebody must've stole it!

01:47.815 --> 01:49.481
You left a couch
out on the curb?

01:49.516 --> 01:51.883
Well, somebody probably thought
it was trash and took it.

01:51.919 --> 01:54.252
You said you were gonna bring
the couch right back in!

01:54.288 --> 01:56.922
What were you thinking?
I'll tell you what I was thinking.

01:56.957 --> 01:59.091
I was thinking we lived
in a safe neighborhood.

01:59.126 --> 02:00.725
But apparently,
I was wrong!

02:00.761 --> 02:03.728
Wait, you're saying
you were wr-wr...

02:03.764 --> 02:04.996
wr-wro...

02:05.032 --> 02:06.264
wr-wrrr...

02:06.300 --> 02:08.934
Oh, I get it--
the Fonz can't say "wrong."

02:08.969 --> 02:12.237
No, Peter, he's 70--
he's having a stroke.

02:17.044 --> 02:18.910
Wow, Peter, I think
starting a community watch

02:18.946 --> 02:19.818
is a great idea.

02:19.843 --> 02:21.701
Yeah, I even got shirts
made up for us.

02:22.382 --> 02:23.648
This is quality work.

02:23.684 --> 02:25.984
Where did you get these?
Via the Web?

02:26.019 --> 02:27.185
Hey, listen, Joe, um,

02:27.221 --> 02:29.187
you think you
can get us all guns?

02:29.223 --> 02:30.689
No, Peter,
they're too dangerous.

02:30.724 --> 02:32.991
<i>Besides, you can't
just go get a gun,</i>

02:33.026 --> 02:35.193
you have to be certified
in gun safety,

02:35.229 --> 02:37.377
go through an extensive
background screening process.

02:37.378 --> 02:38.064
Got 'em.

02:38.065 --> 02:40.031
Whoa. How'd you
get 'em so quick?

02:40.067 --> 02:42.367
Eh, it was easy-- like
pressing that "easy" button

02:42.402 --> 02:44.202
at the office
supply store.

02:44.238 --> 02:46.037
Hey, thanks for all your help.
No problem.

02:46.073 --> 02:47.800
Why don't you go ahead
and hit the "easy" button.

02:47.824 --> 02:49.104
Okay.

02:50.077 --> 02:53.011
What did I just do?
Don't worry about it.

02:56.917 --> 02:59.484
Hey, Quagmire,
you're a sex guy.

02:59.520 --> 03:02.687
You watch any good,
uh... pornos lately?

03:02.723 --> 03:04.956
I mean...
I-I guess.

03:04.992 --> 03:06.525
So what's your pleasure?

03:06.560 --> 03:08.193
What kind of
movies you like?

03:08.228 --> 03:10.529
I don't know.
MILF stuff's kind of cool.

03:10.564 --> 03:12.464
What-what about you?

03:12.499 --> 03:14.933
Me? I have very
particular tastes.

03:14.968 --> 03:17.402
I like a soapy bottom.
What?

03:17.437 --> 03:19.070
Soft-core
soaped-up butts,

03:19.106 --> 03:21.072
like from a PG-13
camp movie.

03:21.108 --> 03:23.508
I can't get enough of it.
Drives me wild.

03:23.544 --> 03:25.343
Okay, let's talk
about something else.

03:25.379 --> 03:28.446
All right. Uh...

03:28.482 --> 03:30.615
it's kind of too cool
for the air-conditioner

03:30.651 --> 03:32.584
and too warm for
the heater, huh?

03:33.921 --> 03:36.721
Ah, got to walk
that boner off, huh?

03:36.757 --> 03:38.356
Yeah.

03:41.295 --> 03:43.161
Hey, guys, you
better come with me.

03:43.197 --> 03:45.597
There's some weird, big-nose
guy hiding in the bushes

03:45.632 --> 03:47.566
outside some
chick's house.

03:48.969 --> 03:51.436
"My heart always
timidly hides itself

03:51.471 --> 03:53.071
behind my mind."

03:54.308 --> 03:56.274
"I set out
to bring down stars

03:56.310 --> 03:57.542
from the sky..."

03:58.579 --> 04:00.278
"Ow. Ow.

04:00.314 --> 04:03.148
"Oh, my God,
four men are beating me.

04:03.183 --> 04:05.550
"My arm.
I think it is broken.

04:05.586 --> 04:07.052
"Who are you guys?

04:07.087 --> 04:08.587
"Why? Why?

04:08.622 --> 04:12.057
"I'll give you anything if
you would only stop hitting me.

04:12.092 --> 04:14.059
"Please stop pulling my nose.

04:14.094 --> 04:15.460
"It is not fake.

04:15.495 --> 04:17.295
"I think I am dying.

04:17.331 --> 04:19.931
Please take me to the hospital."

04:19.967 --> 04:21.600
Your words have bewitched me.

04:21.635 --> 04:23.602
I need your arms around me.

04:23.637 --> 04:25.470
Come to
my chamber at once.

04:25.505 --> 04:27.005
"Come to my chamber
at once."

04:27.040 --> 04:30.642
And bring pound cake.
"And bring pound cake."

04:34.514 --> 04:35.947
Peter, please
come to bed.

04:35.983 --> 04:37.482
Enough of the
community watch.

04:37.517 --> 04:39.818
We live on a very
safe street.

04:39.853 --> 04:42.254
Lois, you wouldn't believe
the things we see out there.

04:42.289 --> 04:45.290
There was a kid riding his bike
while holding a tennis racket.

04:45.325 --> 04:47.792
For real.
Come on! Let's fool around,

04:47.828 --> 04:49.261
or watch a movie,

04:49.296 --> 04:52.197
or finally click that
"Crackle" icon on the TV.

04:52.232 --> 04:54.532
Lois, I am
an unelected vigilante,

04:54.568 --> 04:56.801
and I take my job
very seriously.

04:56.837 --> 04:58.803
Like Serious George.

04:58.839 --> 05:00.705
Hey, George, want
to go to the park?

05:00.741 --> 05:02.540
Uh, thank you, but no.

05:02.576 --> 05:05.076
It's a beautiful day--
lots of mischief to get into.

05:05.112 --> 05:06.344
I don't doubt that,

05:06.380 --> 05:08.380
but as you can see,
I'm pretty busy.

05:08.415 --> 05:10.849
I'm trying to get
a head start on my taxes.

05:10.884 --> 05:13.351
Oh, I see-- trying
to figure out a way

05:13.387 --> 05:15.053
<i>to deduct bananas?</i>

05:15.088 --> 05:17.822
Ah. 'Cause I eat
bananas. Terrific.

05:17.858 --> 05:20.392
Hey, your inside,
so don't wear a hat.

05:20.427 --> 05:23.828
Unless you're leaving,
which would be terrific also.

05:32.105 --> 05:34.072
What the hell? Hey, you!

05:35.776 --> 05:37.409
Step away from that table.

05:37.444 --> 05:40.979
Brain fart. Window. Sorry.

05:41.848 --> 05:43.048
Hold it right there!

05:43.083 --> 05:46.584
I'm warning you!
Hands where I could see 'em.

05:53.760 --> 05:55.727
♪ ♪

05:55.762 --> 05:57.262
Cleveland Jr.?!

05:57.297 --> 05:59.764
Mr. Griffin! You shot me!

05:59.800 --> 06:01.533
Oh, my God!

06:01.568 --> 06:03.568
Peter, where are you?

06:03.603 --> 06:08.039
<i>Peter? Okay, I'm starting
The Good Wife without you.</i>

06:08.075 --> 06:09.341
Phew! Heh.

06:09.376 --> 06:11.176
Unlike you,
I just dodged a bullet.

06:17.401 --> 06:21.169
Okay, next is the...
brown family.

06:21.204 --> 06:23.638
Oh. Oh, my goodness.
I'm-I'm so sorry.

06:23.772 --> 06:25.939
Sometimes I write
descriptions of my patients

06:25.974 --> 06:27.407
to help me
remember them.

06:27.443 --> 06:30.077
No, it's okay.
Our last name is Brown.

06:30.112 --> 06:31.378
Oh, okay. Phew.

06:31.413 --> 06:34.214
Ah, then this must be
"Chubster Dumb-Dumb."

06:35.584 --> 06:37.384
I'm sorry, sir. No visitors.

06:37.419 --> 06:40.454
Excuse me, I'll have you know
I'm the shooter!

06:40.489 --> 06:42.022
So, uh, how's he doing?

06:42.057 --> 06:44.257
"How's he doing"?!
How do you think he's doing!

06:44.293 --> 06:45.926
You shot my son!

06:45.961 --> 06:47.427
Look, Cleveland,
I-I'm real sorry.

06:47.463 --> 06:50.530
I thought someone was breaking
into your house, and I panicked.

06:50.566 --> 06:52.332
It was dark. I-I...
I don't know why

06:52.368 --> 06:53.867
he didn't just say
it was him.

06:53.902 --> 06:55.936
I couldn't hear you.
I was listening to music,

06:55.971 --> 06:58.705
I went to turn it down,
and the next thing I know.

06:58.741 --> 07:00.181
you shot me!

07:00.205 --> 07:01.509
Why the hell were you
climbing in the window

07:01.510 --> 07:02.909
of your own house
anyway?

07:02.945 --> 07:04.711
My dad says opening the door

07:04.747 --> 07:06.646
lets out too much
air-conditioning.

07:06.682 --> 07:08.648
I already have a bullet
in my son,

07:08.684 --> 07:10.517
I don't need one
in my wallet.

07:10.552 --> 07:13.153
You wouldn't have fired
that gun if he was white!

07:13.188 --> 07:14.855
That's not true--
I'll shoot anybody.

07:14.890 --> 07:16.256
Joe, give me
your gun.

07:16.291 --> 07:17.657
Here you go...
Hey, wait a second!

07:17.693 --> 07:19.659
Look, let's all just calm down.

07:19.695 --> 07:20.761
Calm down?!

07:20.796 --> 07:22.596
I want this racist
out the room,

07:22.631 --> 07:24.164
and I want him arrested!

07:24.199 --> 07:26.433
Racist? I put these
gloves on for everybody.

07:26.468 --> 07:28.135
Oh, oh, you're
talking to him.

07:28.170 --> 07:30.904
Look, the police department has
deemed the shooting accidental.

07:30.939 --> 07:33.540
Given the circumstances,
Peter was within his rights

07:33.575 --> 07:34.975
to fire his weapon.

07:35.010 --> 07:38.245
<i>And what about my son's rights
not to be shot?!</i>

07:38.280 --> 07:39.746
Look, Cleveland...

07:39.782 --> 07:41.448
Lat... Latisha?

07:41.483 --> 07:43.316
I thought he had a gun.

07:43.352 --> 07:46.086
I'd never want to do anything
to hurt you or your family.

07:46.121 --> 07:47.154
You're my friend.

07:47.189 --> 07:48.321
<i>I was your friend.</i>

07:48.357 --> 07:49.556
Now, get out of here!

07:49.591 --> 07:51.925
You're nothing but
a worthless bigot!

07:55.130 --> 07:56.930
Wow, I really messed up.

07:56.965 --> 08:00.200
I haven't felt this bad since
I drove by that speed sign.

08:08.076 --> 08:09.609
Aw...

08:20.088 --> 08:22.155
Hey, does anybody know
if Cleveland's coming by?

08:22.191 --> 08:24.558
I was hoping to apologize
and collect his deposit

08:24.593 --> 08:27.394
for the community watch shirts.
I talked to him earlier.

08:27.429 --> 08:30.030
He, uh, he doesn't want
to be anywhere near you.

08:30.065 --> 08:32.332
Hey, look-- they're talking
about the shooting.

08:32.367 --> 08:33.633
Good evening.
Two nights ago

08:33.669 --> 08:36.403
there was a shooting right here
in our own backyard.

08:36.438 --> 08:39.773
The victim: a 14-year-old boy
named Cleveland Brown Jr.

08:39.808 --> 08:42.309
Joining me tonight is
his father, Cleveland Brown.

08:42.344 --> 08:45.412
So that's not really Quahog?
It's just a big picture?

08:45.447 --> 08:48.081
Now, Mr. Brown, I understand
you're trying to get the police

08:48.116 --> 08:49.583
to reopen the investigation.

08:49.618 --> 08:51.985
That's right, Tom.
My family and I believe

08:52.020 --> 08:55.355
this shooting was a hate crime,
and we'd like to see Mr. Griffin

08:55.390 --> 08:57.357
held accountable
for his actions.

08:57.392 --> 08:58.959
Hate crime? That's crazy!

08:58.994 --> 09:00.360
<i>I love all people!</i>

09:00.395 --> 09:02.362
I love blacks, I love Asians...

09:02.397 --> 09:04.731
hell, I even love
gay Aborigines.

09:16.745 --> 09:19.212
Wow, this is
just great, Peter.

09:19.248 --> 09:21.448
Everyone in town
hates us now.

09:21.483 --> 09:24.150
The cashier at the grocery store
told her to "push on,"

09:24.186 --> 09:25.652
and then
she snapped her fingers,

09:25.687 --> 09:28.822
and now I think she's my new
favorite lady in the world.

09:28.857 --> 09:31.391
I don't understand.
I'm not a racist.

09:31.426 --> 09:33.693
It's well documented
that my dream three-way

09:33.729 --> 09:36.796
is S. Epatha Merkerson
and CCH Pounder.

09:36.832 --> 09:38.265
S., this is CCH.

09:38.300 --> 09:39.633
CCH, this is S.

09:39.668 --> 09:41.868
It is my intention
that we conduct this

09:41.904 --> 09:44.304
with both sexiness
and dignity.

09:44.339 --> 09:46.006
Peter, this is a
hot-button issue.

09:46.041 --> 09:48.074
I mean, you shot an
African-American kid.

09:48.110 --> 09:50.477
<i>Of course this isn't
just gonna go away.</i>

09:50.512 --> 09:53.046
Well, there's got to be something
I can do to make things right.

09:53.081 --> 09:55.582
I'll just have to prove to everybody
that I'm not a racist.

09:55.617 --> 09:57.817
How are you gonna do that?
Well, for starters,

09:57.853 --> 09:59.619
I'm gonna head over
to the YMCA.

09:59.655 --> 10:01.488
There's nothing
black guys like more

10:01.523 --> 10:04.724
than out-of-shape
indoor-basketball white guys.

10:06.395 --> 10:09.162
Hey! I'm trying
my best here.

10:09.197 --> 10:11.798
And trying is
what matters most of all.

10:11.833 --> 10:12.966
You're right, Peter.

10:13.001 --> 10:14.701
We need to give
you a chance,

10:14.736 --> 10:16.503
no matter what
color your skin is.

10:16.538 --> 10:18.405
Come on, let's
play some ball.

10:19.775 --> 10:23.209
"...and then Peter and his
new friends went for ice cream."

10:23.245 --> 10:24.844
The end.

10:26.048 --> 10:28.715
Okay, kids, are your parents
out of the room?

10:28.750 --> 10:32.953
<i>Good. Let's get back
to Sloppy Floppers magazine.</i>

10:37.526 --> 10:38.992
What are you doing?

10:39.027 --> 10:41.194
Lois, to show I'm in touch
with what it's like

10:41.229 --> 10:43.496
to be African-American,
I am gonna go to the middle

10:43.532 --> 10:46.433
of the town square, get naked
and paint myself brown.

10:46.468 --> 10:48.501
No, no, that's
offensive.

10:48.537 --> 10:50.103
You can't pretend
to be black.

10:50.138 --> 10:51.438
That's a stupid idea.

10:51.473 --> 10:53.206
What?
It's a stupid idea!

10:53.241 --> 10:56.876
You're a stupid man!
A stupid, stupid man!

10:56.912 --> 10:59.713
Ow, you're hurting me!
Stop it, stop it, Lois!

10:59.748 --> 11:02.549
No! I'm so sick
of your crap.

11:02.584 --> 11:04.918
Why do you always
do these stupid things?

11:04.953 --> 11:08.188
And why do you always announce
them to me before you do them?

11:08.223 --> 11:10.757
Are you trying
to get a rise out of me?

11:10.792 --> 11:14.361
Are you happy now?
Is this what you want?

11:14.396 --> 11:15.996
Oh, no,
it's not what I want!

11:16.031 --> 11:19.532
It's not what I want.
I'm sorry, I'm sorry.

11:20.936 --> 11:23.603
It's never been this bad before.
What do we do?

11:23.639 --> 11:26.039
What we always do.

11:26.074 --> 11:29.843
I'm in charge of my head--
that much I know!

11:35.017 --> 11:37.017
What the hell
are you doing on my property?

11:37.052 --> 11:39.085
Look, it's time we
bury the hatchet.

11:39.121 --> 11:40.654
So I brought a bottle
of your favorite booze.

11:40.689 --> 11:43.089
Now let's just have a drink
and put this all behind us.

11:43.125 --> 11:44.758
I don't want
nothing from you.

11:44.793 --> 11:46.559
Well, hold on,
I got something else.

11:46.595 --> 11:48.995
Cigars. We can smoke 'em
together, all happy,

11:49.031 --> 11:51.164
like a bunch of douche bags
outside a wedding.

11:51.199 --> 11:52.465
Peter, get out of here.

11:52.501 --> 11:54.768
I'm never gonna forgive you
for what you did.

11:54.803 --> 11:56.803
Aw, come on.
This'll change your mind.

11:59.641 --> 12:01.641
Oh, my God!
Quick, do something!

12:04.413 --> 12:06.413
It's not working.
Get rid of it!

12:14.022 --> 12:15.655
Get your family
out of that house!

12:15.691 --> 12:17.490
If they don't leave,
they'll die.

12:17.526 --> 12:19.392
Round up your family
and get out

12:19.428 --> 12:20.527
or you're all
gonna be sorry.

12:20.562 --> 12:22.062
Get out, now!

12:23.398 --> 12:25.432
See, kids, I told you
we'd make friends here.

12:25.467 --> 12:28.268
I guess me getting transferred
by the Xerox Corporation

12:28.303 --> 12:30.704
wasn't the worst thing
after all.

12:38.346 --> 12:40.346
Oh, thank God, Joe.

12:40.382 --> 12:42.982
Are you here to give me the
deposit for the shirts?

12:43.018 --> 12:44.951
No, Peter, I'm here to place you
under arrest

12:44.986 --> 12:47.253
for the attempted murder
of Cleveland Junior.

12:47.289 --> 12:49.622
What are you talkin' about?
You know it was an accident.

12:49.658 --> 12:52.225
Yeah, but let's just say,
public opinion has shifted.

12:52.260 --> 12:54.861
And the boys upstairs said
they can no longer ignore it.

12:54.896 --> 12:56.830
Who the hell are
the "boys upstairs?"

12:56.865 --> 12:58.631
I have no idea.
There's no elevator.

12:58.667 --> 12:59.899
But whoever they are,

12:59.935 --> 13:01.801
they're pretty steamed
about this whole thing.

13:03.105 --> 13:04.437
Peter, what-what's
going on?

13:04.473 --> 13:06.039
They're taking me to jail!

13:06.074 --> 13:07.207
Oh, my God!

13:07.242 --> 13:08.541
Don't worry, Dad!

13:08.577 --> 13:11.277
I'll send you a cake
with a file in it!

13:12.781 --> 13:15.648
These are just the owner manuals
for all our kitchen appliances.

13:15.684 --> 13:17.383
Well, guess I finally have time

13:17.419 --> 13:20.019
to learn to reset the clock
on the coffee maker.

13:20.055 --> 13:22.489
<i>He never did.</i>

13:29.209 --> 13:30.908
You're-you're, uh...

13:30.944 --> 13:32.643
you're not gonna
rape me, are you?

13:32.679 --> 13:34.378
Of course I'm not
gonna rape you.

13:34.414 --> 13:36.714
I'm gonna make you
fall in love with me.

13:36.749 --> 13:38.983
Then... we'll
see what happens.

13:39.018 --> 13:42.620
Oh, no.
It's already working.

13:42.655 --> 13:44.755
Griffin, you have a visitor.

13:44.791 --> 13:46.757
Carter? What are
you doing here?

13:46.793 --> 13:48.059
Hello, Griffin.

13:48.094 --> 13:50.194
I'd like to talk to you
about these charges

13:50.230 --> 13:51.629
that have been
brought against you.

13:51.664 --> 13:53.631
Why don't we go somewhere
a little more private?

13:53.666 --> 13:56.734
I, uh, guess I'll see you
in a little bit?

13:56.769 --> 13:58.836
It's gonna feel
like an eternity.

13:58.871 --> 14:02.607
How is it that I'm only
just now meeting you?

14:04.644 --> 14:06.277
Look, Carter, you
got to believe me.

14:06.312 --> 14:08.846
I didn't shoot Cleveland
Junior because he was black!

14:08.881 --> 14:10.748
Hey, you don't have
to tell me that.

14:10.783 --> 14:13.451
But the media's out there
making you look like a monster,

14:13.486 --> 14:16.354
all for exercising
your constitutional rights.

14:16.389 --> 14:17.688
Grover's a monster.

14:17.724 --> 14:19.857
But don't worry.
We're gonna get you out of this.

14:19.892 --> 14:21.525
I'll be damned
if I'm gonna sit back

14:21.561 --> 14:23.594
and let them do this
to one of my own.

14:23.630 --> 14:25.663
What, you mean your family?
Huh?

14:25.698 --> 14:27.198
Oh, yeah, yeah, that.
Yeah, right.

14:27.233 --> 14:29.000
Look, I'm gonna
bail you out of here,

14:29.035 --> 14:31.535
set you up with my lawyer,
and get these charges dropped.

14:31.571 --> 14:32.803
Well, how you gonna do that?

14:32.839 --> 14:34.538
Don't worry.
I'll come up with a good story,

14:34.574 --> 14:35.773
and they'll eat it up.

14:35.808 --> 14:38.009
<i>Not like when I read
my JAG fan fiction</i>

14:38.044 --> 14:40.578
<i>at the NCIS convention.</i>

14:40.613 --> 14:42.113
"JAG stood up and yelled,

14:42.148 --> 14:44.515
"'Objection, Your Honor,
by Navy law.'

14:44.550 --> 14:46.417
"He then turned
to the lady lawyer,

14:46.452 --> 14:48.486
<i>"the gal from the October Maxim,</i>

14:48.521 --> 14:49.887
"who still managed to be hot

14:49.922 --> 14:52.456
"despite her sexless,
pageboy haircut.

14:52.492 --> 14:54.125
Or perhaps because of it."

14:54.160 --> 14:55.593
Boo!
Terrible!

14:55.628 --> 14:58.896
Right branch of the military,
wrong investigative arm!

15:03.569 --> 15:06.537
And I was trying to
get back into my house,

15:06.572 --> 15:09.907
and my neighbor,
Mr. Griffin, shot me.

15:09.942 --> 15:11.876
He said
he felt threatened by me,

15:11.911 --> 15:14.478
and that hurt even worse
than getting shot!

15:14.514 --> 15:16.080
Aw!

15:16.115 --> 15:18.049
Your Honor, permission
to hug the witness?

15:18.084 --> 15:19.617
Granted.

15:22.188 --> 15:23.621
Don't worry,
Mr. Griffin.

15:23.656 --> 15:24.955
You're every bit
as sympathetic

15:24.991 --> 15:26.791
as this chubby-cheeked
cocoa angel.

15:26.826 --> 15:29.060
I haven't been listening.
What's goin' on?

15:29.095 --> 15:30.761
I don't think it's
lost on any of us

15:30.797 --> 15:32.697
that the laws are
written on white paper.

15:32.732 --> 15:35.166
Yeah, white paper.
Check your jacket pocket.

15:35.201 --> 15:37.335
"I don't think it's
lost on any of us

15:37.370 --> 15:39.236
that the laws are
written on white paper."

15:39.272 --> 15:40.671
Hey, look,
I'm just saying,

15:40.707 --> 15:43.307
it's no surprise that
justice isn't colorblind.

15:43.343 --> 15:45.076
Check your other
jacket pocket.

15:45.111 --> 15:46.477
"Hey, look, I'm just saying

15:46.512 --> 15:48.579
it's no surprise that
justice isn't colorblind."

15:48.614 --> 15:49.847
Stewie, you're a jerk!

15:49.882 --> 15:51.282
Check Chris' pocket.

15:51.317 --> 15:52.757
What? There's nothing
in here, and...

15:52.785 --> 15:55.286
Oh, God, the bottom of the
pocket's been cut out!

15:55.321 --> 15:56.554
Thanks, Brian!

15:56.589 --> 15:59.824
I was the mastermind
behind this whole thing!

15:59.859 --> 16:01.759
Your witness.

16:01.794 --> 16:03.327
All right, watch this.

16:03.363 --> 16:06.297
This is where we take control
of the situation.

16:06.332 --> 16:08.666
Mr. Brown, you testified
that you were listening to music

16:08.701 --> 16:10.067
at the time of the shooting.

16:10.103 --> 16:11.268
That's right.

16:11.304 --> 16:14.271
And isn't Jay-Z music?
Yes.

16:14.307 --> 16:17.708
And doesn't he have the lyrics,
"I put the gun to you.

16:17.744 --> 16:19.877
"I'll kill ya, I'll chop ya up,

16:19.912 --> 16:22.646
put ya inside the mattress
like drug money"?

16:24.016 --> 16:27.485
I was listening
to Neil Sedaka's Hanukkah album.

16:27.520 --> 16:29.086
And isn't true
that your last name

16:29.122 --> 16:30.821
is the same
as Chris Brown's?

16:30.857 --> 16:32.790
Yes, but I don't see what--

16:32.825 --> 16:34.892
And what did Chris Brown
do to Rihanna?

16:34.927 --> 16:37.461
He hit her, like,
a hundred times.

16:37.497 --> 16:39.363
Your Honor, I'd like
to enter into evidence

16:39.399 --> 16:41.766
this photo of a
badly beaten Rihanna

16:41.801 --> 16:44.435
<i>as well as this print ad
for the Entourage movie.</i>

16:44.470 --> 16:45.470
Why?!

16:45.505 --> 16:46.871
I can't unsee this!

16:46.906 --> 16:48.139
Who is this for?!

16:48.174 --> 16:49.407
What's he doing?

16:49.442 --> 16:51.409
He's making Cleveland Jr.
look like a thug.

16:51.444 --> 16:52.777
I know.
That's the idea.

16:52.812 --> 16:54.912
You don't want to go
back to jail, do you?

17:00.219 --> 17:01.619
I don't know.

17:01.654 --> 17:03.354
Maybe.

17:03.389 --> 17:06.056
Mr. Brown, please
pick up this knife.

17:06.092 --> 17:07.691
Aah!
He's got a knife!

17:18.237 --> 17:19.570
This isn't fair!

17:19.605 --> 17:22.006
They're making my son
look like a common hoodlum!

17:22.041 --> 17:23.441
Joe, you're a cop!

17:23.476 --> 17:24.742
Do something!

17:24.777 --> 17:26.844
No, the soap
covers everything.

17:26.879 --> 17:29.713
You might see, like, the
very top of the crack,

17:29.749 --> 17:32.516
but that's-that's
not what it's about.

17:36.456 --> 17:39.290
How do you sleep
at night?

17:39.325 --> 17:41.525
Propped up on pillows,
on account of my fat throat.

17:41.561 --> 17:43.661
If I lay flat on
my back, I die.

17:43.696 --> 17:46.230
I need pillows
between my thighs myself.

17:46.265 --> 17:48.432
And this friendship
is over!

17:58.110 --> 18:00.778
Thanks for letting me
sit in the back.

18:00.813 --> 18:02.346
I was flipping people
off the whole way.

18:04.851 --> 18:06.851
Get out of here,
all of you!

18:06.886 --> 18:10.488
My son didn't do
anything wrong!

18:13.526 --> 18:16.794
Carter, I think this has
all kind of gone too far.

18:16.829 --> 18:17.795
What do you think
you're doing?

18:17.830 --> 18:20.097
I'm gonna make this right.

18:21.167 --> 18:22.833
Everyone!
Everyone!

18:22.869 --> 18:24.902
Listen, I have
something to say.

18:24.937 --> 18:27.638
Cleveland Jr. doesn't
deserve any of this.

18:27.673 --> 18:29.940
All those things you heard
about Cleveland Jr. were lies.

18:29.976 --> 18:32.343
He didn't do anything to me.

18:32.378 --> 18:34.612
He's a good kid,
from a good family.

18:34.647 --> 18:37.948
I just got scared,
and I did something stupid.

18:37.984 --> 18:40.224
I swear, it had nothing to do
with the color of his skin,

18:40.253 --> 18:43.454
but... I did shoot him.

18:44.824 --> 18:48.192
I deserve to be held
responsible for my actions.

18:48.227 --> 18:50.661
Even if that means
going to jail.

18:50.696 --> 18:51.829
You heard him,
other cops.

18:51.864 --> 18:53.597
Let's take him in.

18:53.633 --> 18:55.065
He doesn't know
our names, does he?

18:55.101 --> 18:56.700
I don't think he does.

19:00.406 --> 19:01.605
Wait a minute.

19:01.641 --> 19:03.607
Peter didn't shoot my son.

19:03.643 --> 19:05.175
I did.

19:06.379 --> 19:08.312
Peter was just taking
the blame for me.

19:08.347 --> 19:11.048
He's a good friend.

19:11.083 --> 19:14.385
Eh, Mr. Brown,
what exactly are you saying?

19:14.420 --> 19:16.420
I'm saying that I,
Cleveland Brown,

19:16.455 --> 19:17.888
a black man,

19:17.924 --> 19:19.523
shot Cleveland Brown, Jr.,

19:19.559 --> 19:21.825
another black man.

19:25.064 --> 19:26.630
Wait, wh-where
did everybody go?

19:26.666 --> 19:28.399
You want to make
the media go away?

19:28.434 --> 19:31.168
Just mention
black-on-black crime.

19:31.203 --> 19:33.337
Boy, the world
we live in, huh?

19:33.372 --> 19:35.739
Brian, reach into
Meg's pocket.

19:35.775 --> 19:37.141
Go ahead, Brian.

19:37.176 --> 19:39.843
I-I-I don't want to.

19:39.879 --> 19:42.079
Cleveland,
why did you do that?

19:42.114 --> 19:45.182
Peter, since this is about
racism, why don't we take

19:45.217 --> 19:49.119
a slow, hands-clasped-behind-
the-back walk together?

19:49.155 --> 19:51.322
Listen, I know you wouldn't
have shot Cleveland Jr.

19:51.357 --> 19:53.257
on account of his race.

19:53.292 --> 19:55.225
You shot him because
you're stupid.

19:55.261 --> 19:57.661
That's all
I'm trying to say!

19:57.697 --> 19:59.763
And I know you don't
have hate in your heart.

19:59.799 --> 20:02.299
You were willing to go to jail
for shooting my son.

20:02.335 --> 20:04.535
You took responsibility.

20:04.570 --> 20:06.870
That's what's important.

20:06.906 --> 20:09.239
So... you forgive me?

20:09.275 --> 20:11.408
Of course I do.

20:11.444 --> 20:14.678
Oh, thanks, Cleveland.

20:14.714 --> 20:16.447
Hey, how you
feeling there, champ?

20:16.482 --> 20:17.681
I'm good.

20:17.717 --> 20:19.183
Getting better
every day.

20:19.218 --> 20:20.684
Aw, I'm happy
to hear that.

20:20.720 --> 20:23.754
Look, I-I hope
you know I'm sorry.

20:23.789 --> 20:25.556
Hey, these things happen.

20:25.591 --> 20:27.458
That's my boy.

20:29.629 --> 20:31.362
Mr. Griffin?
Yeah?

20:31.397 --> 20:32.596
Just so you know,

20:32.632 --> 20:34.531
I'm gonna be coming
for your ass.

20:34.567 --> 20:36.133
Wh-What's that now?

20:36.168 --> 20:37.635
I'm saying it's on!

20:37.670 --> 20:39.637
You ever feel the cool steel

20:39.672 --> 20:42.673
of a switchblade
pressed against your temple?

20:43.776 --> 20:45.943
He Mr. Griffin,

20:45.978 --> 20:47.444
I'm just kidding.

20:47.480 --> 20:48.612
Or am I?

20:48.648 --> 20:51.015
You're gonna wonder about that,
you fat bitch.

20:51.050 --> 20:51.906
See you later!

20:51.907 --> 20:55.407
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru